   "text": "NaHoO2 (mp-755141) is clearly present; CaAl2O4 (mp-558636) as the second phase is a tentative call. I worked from about seven peak positions below 40\u00b0 only.\n\n**NaHoO2.** Its primitive cell converts to a body-centred tetragonal cell with a \u2248 4.61 \u00c5 and c \u2248 10.33 \u00c5. Its main reflections line up with the strongest observed peaks:\n\n| Reflection | Calculated d (\u00c5) | Observed d (\u00c5) | Observed peak (2\u03b8, intensity) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| (101) | 4.21 | 4.15 | 21.4\u00b0, 100 |\n| (103)/(112) | \u22482.76 | 2.716 | 32.95\u00b0 |\n| (004) | 2.58 | 2.544 | 35.25\u00b0 |\n| (200) | 2.305 | 2.271 | 39.65\u00b0 |\n\nEvery observed d is about 1.5% smaller than calculated, a uniform offset that suggests a slightly contracted lattice rather than a wrong match.\n\n**Unassigned peaks.** NaHoO2 has no reflections at 12.7\u00b0 (d \u2248 6.96 \u00c5), 28.7\u00b0 (d \u2248 3.11 \u00c5) or 30.05\u00b0 (d \u2248 2.97 \u00c5).\n\n- **CaAl2O4 fits these best.** Its (001) is at 6.98 \u00c5, (110) at 3.13 \u00c5 and (111) at 2.98 \u00c5.\n  - Against this, it also predicts peaks near 22.4\u00b0 and 23.35\u00b0 (d \u2248 3.97 and 3.81 \u00c5) that are not visible.\n- **Nd2SbO2 explains 12.7\u00b0 and 30.05\u00b0 only if contracted like NaHoO2.** It cannot account for 28.7\u00b0, and it predicts a strong 31.6\u00b0 peak that is absent.\n- **The other six candidates do not fit.** ErMnO3, Rb2O, BaEuFe2O5, Mn2V3NiO8 and Na2NiO3 predict strong lines where the pattern has none. Na2Ni3O5 is triclinic and I did not test it.\n\n{\"present\": [\"mp-755141\", \"mp-558636\"], \"confidence\": 0.6, \"note\": \"NaHoO2 matches the main peaks with a uniform ~1.5% d-spacing contraction, while the weaker peaks at 12.7, 28.7 and 30.05 deg best fit CaAl2O4, though that second phase is tentative.\"}",
